ry\n\nI've created two fully functional scripts in `/app`:\n\n### **compress.py**\nReshards a dataset according to your constraints:\n- **Max 30 items per directory**: Creates hierarchical `shard_0/`, `shard_1/`, etc.\n- **Max 15MB per file**: Combines original files into `combined_*.bin` chunks\n- **Metadata tracking**: Stores `.reshard_metadata.json` with the mapping of original files to their locations (shard, chunk, offset, size)\n- **Preserves directory structure**: Handles nested directories correctly\n\n### **decompress.py**\nRestores the original file structure in-place:\n- Reads the metadata file\n- Extracts each original file from its chunk using the stored offset and size\n- Recreates the exact original directory structure and file contents\n\n### **Testing Results**\n✅ Successfully resharded 9,898 JSONL files (800MB) from flat structure into hierarchical shards\n- shard_0: 30 combined files (~15MB each)\n- shard_1: 23 combined files (~15MB each)\n\n✅ Decompression perfectly restored all files\n- All checksums match originals exactly\n- Nested directory structures work correctly\n- Total roundtrip: compress → decompress = perfect fidelity\n\n### **Usage**\n```bash\n# Setup environment\nuv sync\n\n# Compress\npython /app/compress.py <input_dir> <output_dir>\n\n# Decompress (in-place)\npython /app/decompress.py <resharded_dir>\n\n# Or with uv run\nuv run python compress.py <input_dir> <output_dir>\nuv run python decompress.py <resharded_dir>\n```\n\nThe scripts are generic and ready for your other data slices!","ttft_ms":2356,"type":"result","duration_ms":118517,"uuid":"7b2fa7f3-ebd0-45ce-9537-15780e4f8cc3","ttft_stream_ms":993,"time_to_request_ms":92,"queued_turn_count":0}
